  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-104(c)(1)): (c) (1) A person may not store or leave a firearm in a location where the person knew or should have known that an unsupervised MINOR COULD gain access to the firearm.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-104(c)(2)): (2) A PERSON MAY NOT STORE OR LEAVE A FIREARM IN A LOCATION WHERE: (I) THE PERSON KNEW OR SHOULD HAVE KNOWN THAT AN UNSUPERVISED MINOR COULD GAIN ACCESS TO THE FIREARM; AND (II) AN UNSUPERVISED MINOR DOES GAIN ACCESS TO THE FIREARM.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-104(c)(3)): (3) A PERSON MAY NOT STORE OR LEAVE A FIREARM IN A LOCATION WHERE: (I) THE PERSON KNEW OR SHOULD HAVE KNOWN THAT AN UNSUPERVISED MINOR COULD GAIN ACCESS TO THE FIREARM; (II) AN UNSUPERVISED MINOR DOES GAIN ACCESS TO THE FIREARM; AND (III) THE FIREARM CAUSES HARM TO THE MINOR OR TO ANOTHER PERSON.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-104(d)): (d) (1) A person who violates SUBSECTION (C)(1) OF this section is guilty of a misdemeanor and on conviction is subject to a fine not exceeding $1,000 (2) A PERSON WHO VIOLATES SUBSECTION (C)(2) OF THIS SECTION IS GUILTY OF A MISDEMEANOR AND ON CONVICTION IS SUBJECT TO IMPRISONMENT NOT EXCEEDING 1 YEAR OR A FINE NOT EXCEEDING $2,500 OR BOTH. (3) A PERSON WHO VIOLATES SUBSECTION (C)(3) OF THIS SECTION IS GUILTY OF A MISDEMEANOR AND ON CONVICTION IS SUBJECT TO IMPRISONMENT NOT EXCEEDING 3 YEARS OR A FINE NOT EXCEEDING $5,000 OR BOTH."
}